Main: { .main(s: mut System): Void }
/// A `Main` implementing ``OpenWith[I,E]`` asks the Fearless manager to run it on a double click
/// on any file with the extension ``E``, and to show those files with the icon ``I``:
/// ``Foo: Main, OpenWith[IconsFoo,"foo"]{ s -> ... }`` opens every ``.foo`` file.
/// ``I`` is a type generated for an autoloaded image file, like ``IconsFoo`` for
/// ``_pkg/icons/foo.png``, or `IconsConflict`; the manager accepts only a square PNG image with a
/// side from 64 to 1024 pixels. ``E`` is a string literal type holding the extension without its
/// dot: 1 to 16 characters, each a lowercase letter or a digit; ``"fearless"`` is reserved.
/// A Fearless extension, ``"ffile"`` followed by three digits, is taken by the manager outright;
/// any other, a system extension like ``"htm"``, only once the user allowed it in the manager.
/// ``"fapp"`` followed by three digits names shortcut files and is refused here.
/// Only a `Main` can implement it, and a `Main` claims each extension at most once across all its
/// `OpenWith[_,_]` and `Shortcut[_,_]`. The portable Fearless ignores it.
OpenWith[I,E]: {}
/// ``OpenWith[I]`` is `OpenWith[_,_]` with an extension chosen by the Fearless manager, like
/// ``ffile042``: users recognise those files by the icon ``I``, not by their extension.
OpenWith[I]: {}
/// A `Main` implementing ``Shortcut[I,E]`` asks the Fearless manager to create a file
/// ``name.E`` in the top level of its project, showing the icon ``I``, that runs the main on a
/// double click, also when moved somewhere else: ``Bar: Main, Shortcut[IconsBar,"fapp123"]{ s -> ... }``
/// gets the file ``bar.fapp123``. ``name`` is the simple name of the main turned into a file name:
/// ``FooBar`` gives ``foo_bar``. ``I`` is as in `OpenWith[_,_]`. ``E`` is ``"fapp"`` followed by
/// three digits, like ``"fapp042"``: the shortcut file never looks like a document of another
/// program or a file of the project. The portable Fearless ignores it.
Shortcut[I,E]: {}
/// ``Shortcut[I]`` is `Shortcut[_,_]` with an extension chosen by the Fearless manager, like
/// ``fapp042``: users recognise the shortcut file by the icon ``I``, not by its extension.
Shortcut[I]: {}
Sealed: {}
Void: Sealed {}
WidenTo[T]: {}
InferUnknown: Sealed {}
InferErr[A,B]: Sealed {}
InferErr[A,B,C]: Sealed {}
InferErr[A,B,C,D]: Sealed {}

ToIso[R]: {mut .iso: iso ToIso[R]; mut .close: mut R;}

Abort: Sealed {![R:**]: R -> _Throw.nonDeterministic(Infos.msg "Abort reached");}
_Magic: Sealed {
  ![R:**]: R -> this!; // magic'd out to tell us what we forgot to implement
  //![R:**](_: mut _System): R -> _Throw.nonDeterministic(Infos.msg `Abort reached`);
  }

_MagicDebug: Sealed {
  #(x: read ToStr): Void -> _Magic!;
  }

///Prints the string representation of x, followed by a newline.
///It can be called from any code, with no capability: the program has no way to observe what was printed.
Debug: Sealed {
  #[T](x: T, f: ToStrBy[T]): T -> Block#(this#(f#x.str),x);
  #(x: read ToStr): Void -> _MagicDebug# x;
  //.identify[T](x: read T): Str -> _Magic!;//TODO: can this break observability?
  }

BaseId[T1:*,T2]: CaptureFree{ #(x: T1): T2 }
BaseContainer[T1:*]: Sealed{
  read .as[T2](f: BaseId[read/imm T1,T2]): BaseContainer[T2];
  imm  .as[T2](f: BaseId[imm T1,T2]): BaseContainer[T2];
  }

